WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.029
The storms were unlike anything anyone had
ever seen.

00:00:04.029 --> 00:00:09.019
But the worst part wasn’t just the deadly
gales, wind howling powerful enough to knock

00:00:09.019 --> 00:00:13.909
down buildings like rows of dominoes, and
lift the remaining debris of cities up into

00:00:13.909 --> 00:00:17.120
the air as if all that destruction weighed
nothing.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:22.150
And it wasn’t just the lightning, those
arcs of crimson forking down from above.

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:26.210
If one struck the ground near you – and
one almost always did – the sheer force

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:28.310
of it would knock you off your feet.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:32.300
The last thing you’d feel as you flailed
helplessly in the air was the relentless pain

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:37.470
of your body being disintegrated by the energy
of the blood-red lightning, until there was

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.510
nothing left of you for anyone to find.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:43.600
Yet, somehow that wasn’t the worst part
either.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.989
And it wasn’t even the noise of it all either,
that deafening cacophony of booming thunder

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:54.110
and wild, hurricane-force winds, so loud nobody
could ignore it, all underscored by the screams

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:57.020
of a world lost in suffering and madness.

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.970
No, the worst part of it all was the sky.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:04.470
Whenever anyone looked up, where there had
once been that clear, calming blue, was now

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:07.450
a swirling mass of nightmares.

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:12.890
Many were surprised just how much they missed
turning to the sky, that odd, universal comfort

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:17.790
it brought, the knowledge that no matter how
bleak things got, the sun would set on every

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:22.979
bad day and rise again to mark the start of
another, filled with potential.

00:01:22.979 --> 00:01:29.630
That promise of a future, no matter how uncertain,
was replaced with a reminder of one thing:

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:32.590
that this new, darker day had no end.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:36.950
There was no sunrise or sunset, no night or
day.

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:42.479
All that uncertainty and potential was replaced
with certain doom, represented by a sky that

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:44.850
looked like a river of blood.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:49.490
Deep reds and blacks swirled and thrashed
above like the raging waves of the ocean,

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:53.950
casting bolts of lightning down at the Earth…
not to mention what else would occasionally

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:56.580
drop from that bloodstained sky.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:00.600
Nobody had much information about how this
had all started, how the world had become

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.270
such an unrecognizable hellscape.

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:07.950
Cynics would say that the world was already
hell long before the sky turned red, although

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:11.980
there wasn’t much time for sarcastic jokes
like that nowadays.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:16.830
As far as the few human beings that had survived
could remember, the day everything changed

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:20.600
had been little more than an ordinary day
on Planet Earth.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:25.380
One moment things were normal, people were
working tirelessly at their boring nine-to-five

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:30.400
jobs, somewhere in the world others had long
since fallen asleep in a different time zone.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.780
Then, all of a sudden, it appeared.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:39.330
Few survivors had actually seen it for themselves,
and even fewer had lived to tell the tale.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:43.910
But rumors and whispers spread from camp to
camp, dispossessed people huddled together

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:49.120
in the ruins of houses or in abandoned subway
tunnels would hear the stories.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:54.900
And somehow, deep down in the fearful recesses
of their hearts, they all knew, despite never

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.390
having seen it, that it was real… the Masked
God.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:03.500
When it stepped upon the earth, it walked
like any other person would; its body even

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.890
appeared to be human.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:10.349
An aged, older man’s body, wrinkled and
elderly, although not completely decrepit.

00:03:10.349 --> 00:03:16.640
Yet it was his face, or what covered it, that
really instilled that sense of fear and dread

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.910
in anyone that heard the rumors.

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:25.390
The being wore a mask, a porcelain comedy
mask, the kind commonly associated with Ancient

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:26.500
Greek theatre.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:31.050
It had a fixed, unnerving expression, a wide
smile of twisted glee.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:35.460
It was almost as if it was getting some sick
enjoyment out of all the chaos and destruction

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:37.360
that had befallen the world…

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.230
like it was pleased with its own handiwork.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:45.180
A thick, black substance oozed from the mask
too, adding to its unsettling appearance as

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:49.420
streaks of what looked like tar trickled down
the chalky white surface.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:54.040
It leaked out from underneath as well, dripping
over the bony shoulders of the old man that

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:55.040
wore it.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:59.980
Not one survivor that heard the stories of
this monster understood what it was or where

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:05.410
it had come from, but – as if by some deific
influence – they all knew it was responsible

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:08.080
for creating the hell they now lived in.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:14.310
That knowledge kept them hidden, kept them
afraid… and kept them from fighting back.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:18.949
As had always been the case, even before this
apocalypse had been unleashed on the world,

00:04:18.949 --> 00:04:23.669
the only people who knew the truth were those
who had been working for the SCP Foundation.

00:04:23.669 --> 00:04:28.550
They had more than their fair share of answers
about what had happened, and who – or what

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:33.870
– this mask-wearing menace was, but naturally
kept that information secret from the wider

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:34.870
world.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:38.600
Not that there was much point in keeping secrets
anymore; after all, there was hardly much

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:43.539
of a world left for the Foundation to hide
things from… and even fewer former personnel

00:04:43.539 --> 00:04:45.520
who had lasted this long.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:49.339
Even then, there was only a handful at the
SCP Foundation who knew everything that had

00:04:49.339 --> 00:04:51.800
led to the current catastrophe.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:56.169
Most of the researchers and guards had been
going about their ordinary duties, running

00:04:56.169 --> 00:05:00.960
tests on contained anomalies or patrolling
the site where a certain, Possessive Mask

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.159
was housed.

00:05:02.159 --> 00:05:06.340
The next thing everyone there knew was the
blaring noise of emergency alarms, Mobile

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:09.139
Task Force troopers racing down the hallways.

00:05:09.139 --> 00:05:12.849
Their commander might have yelled something
about a break in, someone having gained access

00:05:12.849 --> 00:05:17.949
to the supposedly secure Foundation facility
and stealing one of their anomalous objects.

00:05:17.949 --> 00:05:22.819
But not everybody, even those working in the
same building, would have overheard that.

00:05:22.819 --> 00:05:25.849
They definitely didn’t miss what happened
next, though.

00:05:25.849 --> 00:05:30.939
As further alarms sounded, alerting the staff
on-site of a containment breach, the facility

00:05:30.939 --> 00:05:34.719
itself was torn apart in a flurry of chaos.

00:05:34.719 --> 00:05:40.589
Personnel – researchers, security, MTF soldiers
– were being incinerated, burned until there

00:05:40.589 --> 00:05:43.310
was literally no trace of them left.

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:48.129
Something stepped through the very brickwork
of the building itself, smashing a hole through

00:05:48.129 --> 00:05:51.949
every room it passed until it burst out of
the side.

00:05:51.949 --> 00:05:56.400
Then, all of a sudden, the alarms weren’t
the loudest sound, something else started

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:59.460
deafening the Foundation staff who were still
standing.

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:05.729
The world outside had become even more chaotic;
the sky had turned red and, all around, people

00:06:05.729 --> 00:06:10.849
were being killed, structures decimated, cities
blown away in moments.

00:06:10.849 --> 00:06:14.740
Naturally, this wasn’t the first time the
Foundation had stared right into the face

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:17.500
of an XK Class end-of-the-world scenario.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:22.160
Given the widespread presence and surveillance
they had around the planet, it didn’t take

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:25.120
them long to learn of the horrors that were
unfolding.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:31.580
The key word there was that they had a widespread
presence, as in past tense.

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:35.080
They thought they had enough resources to
retaliate too.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:39.189
Word quickly spread throughout the various
arms of the SCP Foundation, informing the

00:06:39.189 --> 00:06:44.419
wider organization of the situation and urging
them to work as one to enact a plan to stop

00:06:44.419 --> 00:06:45.840
what was happening.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:51.090
All they knew for certain was that SCP-035
had been removed from containment.

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:55.540
Also known as the Possessive Mask, the object
was known to have its own sentience and an

00:06:55.540 --> 00:07:00.169
innate ability to telepathically influence
unwitting victims into wearing it.

00:07:00.169 --> 00:07:04.869
However, the mask also secreted a corrosive
black substance, which normally dissolved

00:07:04.869 --> 00:07:07.029
the body of anyone who put it on.

00:07:07.029 --> 00:07:12.960
By itself, SCP-035 was nowhere near powerful
enough to unleash a global catastrophe though.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:17.349
Unfortunately, it had managed to influence
someone who was that powerful into putting

00:07:17.349 --> 00:07:19.759
it on; another anomaly.

00:07:19.759 --> 00:07:26.639
While, to the untrained eye, SCP-343 could
easily be mistaken for an elderly human man,

00:07:26.639 --> 00:07:30.860
those at the Foundation knew that the fact
he was now wearing the Possessive Mask was

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:34.699
some of the worst news they could have ever
received.

00:07:34.699 --> 00:07:39.300
Although none of the researchers working for
the SCP Foundation – in fact, not even the

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:46.169
O5 Council – knew if this was true, the
colloquial nickname for SCP-343 was ‘God’.

00:07:46.169 --> 00:07:50.979
He not only claimed to be the sole creator
of the entire universe, but had also exhibited

00:07:50.979 --> 00:07:56.169
extensive reality-warping abilities, advanced
even for an anomalous being.

00:07:56.169 --> 00:08:00.889
His powers seemingly had no known limit in
how they could be used to alter the world

00:08:00.889 --> 00:08:06.429
around him, although the old man himself seemed
to be a passive, kindly soul, rarely causing

00:08:06.429 --> 00:08:10.300
active harm to other beings under normal circumstances.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:16.649
Of course, normal circumstances didn’t include
having the corruptive SCP-035 on his face,

00:08:16.649 --> 00:08:22.499
effectively putting the mask in the driver’s
seat, and allowing it to use SCP-343’s powers

00:08:22.499 --> 00:08:25.119
to lay waste to anything before it.

00:08:25.119 --> 00:08:29.999
The Foundation quickly diverted their considerable
assets to a brute force retaliation, in the

00:08:29.999 --> 00:08:34.579
hopes that a full-scale assault on the combined
creature would somehow force a separation

00:08:34.579 --> 00:08:36.870
of the Possessive Mask from SCP-343’s face.

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:43.140
The tricky thing about this situation was,
‘God’s powers and the fact that he was

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:48.490
an immortal, ageless being of potentially
incomprehensible form, all meant he couldn’t

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:49.870
be harmed.

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:53.269
Causing external damage to him was extremely
difficult.

00:08:53.269 --> 00:08:58.579
That was good news in some regard, after all,
the Foundation didn’t want to kill 343 if

00:08:58.579 --> 00:09:02.529
they could help it; they knew he wasn’t
acting of his own accord.

00:09:02.529 --> 00:09:07.980
But his indestructibility also meant that
the corrosive goo that was secreted from SCP-035

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:12.060
had little to no effect on its new, impervious
host.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:17.639
That meant it could keep going, keep unleashing
hell, and stopping it was going to take a

00:09:17.639 --> 00:09:19.579
lot of manpower.

00:09:19.579 --> 00:09:24.889
Fortunately, the SCP Foundation never had
any shortage of people to throw at a problem,

00:09:24.889 --> 00:09:28.480
and their ethos didn’t really place much
value on human life.

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:32.940
They mobilized every Mobile Task Force at
their disposal, every one of them filled with

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:36.009
ranks of highly trained elite operatives.

00:09:36.009 --> 00:09:40.949
Among the Foundation’s forces were even
MTF agents who had themselves been altered

00:09:40.949 --> 00:09:46.600
through anomalous means, their bodies augmented
with technology and cybernetics, or their

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.149
strength specially enhanced.

00:09:49.149 --> 00:09:53.779
Deploying the full might of their amassed
forces, the SCP Foundation took the fight

00:09:53.779 --> 00:09:59.589
to SCP-035, with the goal of stopping its
reign of terror and freeing SCP-343 if possible.

00:09:59.589 --> 00:10:05.730
The hybridized, mask-wearing reality warper
had already caused considerable damage since

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:07.750
it had started its rampage.

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:12.319
Although its motivations were far from political,
the Wearer of the Anguish Mask had begun with

00:10:12.319 --> 00:10:16.449
a devastating show of power, wiping numerous
cities off the map.

00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:20.980
While the rest of the world scrabbled to find
some way of responding, the Masked God teleported

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:25.730
itself across the globe, destroying the central
governments and further crippling their own

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:29.060
opportunities to initiate an armed response.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:34.019
In short, this meant The Foundation’s move
was to be humanity’s last stand, their final

00:10:34.019 --> 00:10:40.380
chance to stop SCP-035 from its current course
of harnessing the wise old man’s power to

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:44.120
turn the world into its own personal, nightmarish
playground.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:48.899
To say there was a lot riding on the MTF assault
would be an understatement…

00:10:48.899 --> 00:10:51.329
as would saying it went badly.

00:10:51.329 --> 00:10:56.879
When met with times of defeat, the old, rather
morbid adage of fallen soldiers being ‘sent

00:10:56.879 --> 00:10:59.470
home in bags’ is often applied.

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:04.149
But if the masked hybrid had sent the Foundation
its MTF troops back to them encased in body

00:11:04.149 --> 00:11:08.829
bags, then that would have been far kinder
than what it actually did.

00:11:08.829 --> 00:11:14.550
The collected Mobile Task Forces, the Foundation’s
own private army, were mobilized to Washington.

00:11:14.550 --> 00:11:19.779
Under the influence of the Possessive Mask,
SCP-343 had wiped out not only the main seat

00:11:19.779 --> 00:11:25.959
of power in the United States, but the Pentagon
as well, disabling the country’s defenses.

00:11:25.959 --> 00:11:29.810
Suddenly, a mass of aerial transports and
ground vehicles came hurtling towards the

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:35.670
crater it had left behind; as it turned to
look, the wide grin of satisfaction on SCP-035

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.970
became a long frown.

00:11:37.970 --> 00:11:43.110
Thanks to its new host's omniscience, it instantly
recognized the foot soldiers of the organization

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:45.830
that had kept it caged for so long.

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:50.519
As the amassed MTFs marched towards it, the
masked god stepped out to meet the oncoming

00:11:50.519 --> 00:11:55.380
army; one being against thousands of troops
– if not tens of thousands.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:59.689
If the mask had affixed itself to the face
of any other anomaly, those soldiers might

00:11:59.689 --> 00:12:01.800
have stood a slim chance.

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:06.350
The combined creature casually raised the
bony arms of its host body, the Foundation

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:10.269
forces breaking into a charge the very second
that they saw it move.

00:12:10.269 --> 00:12:14.850
Like a tidal wave, they rushed towards their
target, only for each individual operative

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:18.050
to quickly realize that they had stopped moving.

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:23.670
They were still running, legs still in motion,
but their feet had been lifted off the ground.

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:28.040
Plucked from the very earth they had each
stood on, the MTFs were stuck in mid-air,

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:31.899
defying the forces of gravity and unable to
free themselves.

00:12:31.899 --> 00:12:38.560
Collectively, the Foundation’s army looked
to SCP-035, its tragic porcelain frown having

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:44.319
switched back to the wide grin, punctuating
the sick satisfaction it was about to take

00:12:44.319 --> 00:12:45.990
from what came next.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:51.439
It gave a click of God’s lean fingers, and
each of the MTF troops it had suspended in

00:12:51.439 --> 00:12:54.629
mid-air were shredded at the molecular level.

00:12:54.629 --> 00:13:00.130
Their bodies erupted with a spray of deep
red viscera, every one of them being pulled

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:02.680
to pieces from the inside out.

00:13:02.680 --> 00:13:10.379
Flesh, bone, and blood melting away, breaking
down; becoming ash, then atoms, then nothing.

00:13:10.379 --> 00:13:16.209
It took around a minute, not that it was terribly
exerting for SCP-343’s powers, but just

00:13:16.209 --> 00:13:20.230
because of how many troops the Foundation
had sent to try and stop it.

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:23.870
A mighty show of force, and all for nothing.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:29.029
With their Mobile Task Forces decimated like
a row of helpless tin soldiers, the SCP Foundation

00:13:29.029 --> 00:13:31.370
had lost its primary method of fighting back.

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:35.100
But they were far from safe from the masked
god’s reach.

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:42.029
Thanks to its host, SCP-035 wasn’t all-knowing,
but all-seeing and able to be anywhere and

00:13:42.029 --> 00:13:44.160
everywhere in the blink of an eye.

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:48.220
It began hunting the surviving pockets of
the Foundation’s personnel.

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:52.970
Out of nowhere, it would teleport into wherever
they were hiding and turn their bodies inside

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:57.920
out, or rearranging the functions of every
orifice on their faces, only to vanish like

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:02.050
a ghost, leaving no trace… and no survivors.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:06.639
The braver ones tried desperately to come
up with some new plan, a revised way to stop

00:14:06.639 --> 00:14:10.220
a creature that could be anywhere and do anything.

00:14:10.220 --> 00:14:14.089
On the other hand, The Foundation leadership,
the more highly ranked members like the Overwatch

00:14:14.089 --> 00:14:16.389
Council went to the ground.

00:14:16.389 --> 00:14:20.540
Plenty of them had contingency plans in place
for Armageddon, and were prepared to wait

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:23.670
out the apocalypse in their own secluded,
safe haven.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:28.639
But with the Foundation all but gone, that’s
when the monsters got loose.

00:14:28.639 --> 00:14:33.189
No longer having anyone to guard them, to
maintain their specific, specialized containment

00:14:33.189 --> 00:14:38.699
procedures, the SCPs still held at Foundation
sites were unleashed on the world.

00:14:38.699 --> 00:14:43.769
Untold horrors came spilling out of the ruined
facilities, each one now acting as its own

00:14:43.769 --> 00:14:49.509
Pandora’s Box, bursting its lock and having
its terrible contents lay waste to the planet

00:14:49.509 --> 00:14:51.249
already awash with chaos.

00:14:51.249 --> 00:14:57.180
A lot of the anomalies thrived in the world
that SCP-035 had created, once they were finished

00:14:57.180 --> 00:15:01.120
fighting among themselves in the struggle
of escaping their containment.

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:04.180
d7f7db420598360e2837bb6ff8f6f5b840]
Soon, there were packs of SCP-745 running

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:09.589
wild on the ruined highways, using their bioluminescent
lights to hunt human survivors who were attempting

00:15:09.589 --> 00:15:12.620
to make the dangerous trek across open country.

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:17.540
Meanwhile, a plague began spreading among
other camps of these post-apocalyptic humans,

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:22.560
a strange disease that seemed to cause people
to rapidly grow extra teeth, overproducing

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:26.470
them until SCP-4910, the Grinner, could catch
up to them.

00:15:26.470 --> 00:15:31.740
Then, there were the SCPs that fled the nightmare
that the Masked God had made of the world.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:35.790
Any that could travel between dimensions or
remove themselves from this layer of reality

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:38.809
quickly absconded to avoid the chaos.

00:15:38.809 --> 00:15:42.490
Some just went about their business, as if
nothing had really changed.

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:47.379
The Plague Doctor mostly kept to himself,
traveling from place to place on foot, only

00:15:47.379 --> 00:15:52.209
stopping when he encountered people afflicted
with the Pestilence, before moving on in search

00:15:52.209 --> 00:15:53.389
of others.

00:15:53.389 --> 00:15:57.809
Some of the anomalies tried to help people,
rumors spread among some survivor camps of

00:15:57.809 --> 00:16:02.910
a half-man, half-cactus leaving them food
and supplies in the night, with a note that

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:06.139
read ‘From your friendly neighborhood Cactusman.’

00:16:06.139 --> 00:16:10.430
There weren’t many who dared to oppose the
creator of this dark new world.

00:16:10.430 --> 00:16:14.220
But some anomalies sought to challenge the
rule of this combined creature.

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:21.420
Perhaps they thought SCP-035 and SCP-343 couldn’t
possibly be as powerful as the stories said,

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:26.759
that it would be easy to kill the king and
assume control over his kingdom of chaos.

00:16:26.759 --> 00:16:31.880
There were plenty of other anomalies that
had floated the idea, not just the other reality-warpers

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:36.910
but those that had figured out that if they
separated the mask from its host, then this

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:43.199
world would become their hellish paradise
to rule of – so long as SCP-343 didn’t

00:16:43.199 --> 00:16:45.350
instantly undo all the damage.

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:49.920
But there was one that didn’t want control,
it didn’t even necessarily mind that the

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:52.610
whole world had been turned into a waking
nightmare.

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:57.329
It just wanted to stand against the hybrid
of malicious mask and all-powerful deity out

00:16:57.329 --> 00:17:02.730
of spite, based on nothing but pure hatred
for any and all other forms of life other

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:04.050
than itself.

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:09.709
And it was that confrontation that would serve
as a warning to the rest of the SCPs now freely

00:17:09.709 --> 00:17:11.780
roaming the world.

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:17.120
SCP-682 slithered out into the open, claws
coated with a fresh coating of blood from

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:22.069
its latest slaughter, wetting the countless
layers beneath that had already dried.

00:17:22.069 --> 00:17:26.620
The Hard to Destroy Reptile had tracked the
scent of the Possessive Mask’s oozing black

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:31.400
secretions, bringing the beast maw-to-porcelain
face with the combined being responsible for

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:34.320
distorting the very fabric of the world.

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:39.940
Already knowing the foul lizard was near thanks
to its host’s foresight, SCP-035’s visage

00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:44.720
had long been locked in that unhappy grimace,
dreading the approach of the day it would

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:48.940
have to face the tenacious, irritating regenerative
reptile.

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:53.700
It turned its host’s body to face the huge
beast, the trails of black streaked down its

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:58.580
frowning face looking like angry tears staining
its carved, off-white skin.

00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:01.400
The two exchanged no words.

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:07.210
SCP-682 had no doubt this pairing of corruptive
mask and passive god already knew why it had

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:08.770
come looking for it.

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:14.210
And it was right, the Possessive Mask had
long been looking into the mind of SCP-343

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:15.210
to prepare.

00:18:15.210 --> 00:18:19.520
It knew it wasn’t one of the old man’s
children, in fact, God had completely denied

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:23.460
ever being responsible for the creation of
the unkillable monster.

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:28.000
There was almost no strategy, even with the
infinite power of its hosts' reality-warping

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:32.260
abilities, that SCP-035 could definitively
kill SCP-682.

00:18:32.260 --> 00:18:38.740
Building up to a charge, the reptile swiped
at the masked god, its talons narrowly nicking

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:43.059
the porcelain surface of the mask the very
second it teleported out of the way.

00:18:43.059 --> 00:18:48.760
Reappearing behind the monster, SCP-035 compelled
its host body to lift its elderly arm and

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:51.960
decimate the beast the same way it had to
the Foundation forces.

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:56.010
With a fearsome hiss, the reptile’s body
was pulled apart.

00:18:56.010 --> 00:19:00.190
It growled with anger, annoyed and enraged
more than deterred.

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:04.880
Its strong, scaly limbs quickly regenerated,
bone and muscle regrowing to replace what

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:06.590
the masked god had torn away.

00:19:06.590 --> 00:19:13.450
SCP-682 gave a swipe of its tail, knocking
the masked god a few feet away, reeling him.

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:18.970
The anomalous hybrid teleported yet again,
this time to inside the monstrous reptile.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:24.790
Shrinking down to almost infinitely small,
the mask and god wrenched apart SCP-682’s

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:30.890
atoms, ripping up strand after strand of its
very DNA, physically trying to unmake it on

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:32.370
a cellular level.

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:37.100
On the outside, the creature’s body disintegrated
as it roared, feeling its very genetic material

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:44.440
being broken down… only for it to rapidly
reform just as SCP-343, wearing SCP-035, reappeared

00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:45.590
in front of it.

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:50.740
There was no way for the masked god to kill
the monster, despite how much it tried.

00:19:50.740 --> 00:19:54.909
Sending it hurtling into the fire of the Sun,
punching it into other dimensions, moving

00:19:54.909 --> 00:19:59.570
it down the recursive stack of reality to
make its existence little more than fiction.

00:19:59.570 --> 00:20:03.850
Eventually, the Possessive Mask had to reconsider
the problem at hand.

00:20:03.850 --> 00:20:08.860
Even with infinite power, the unkillable still
remained unkillable.

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:13.260
Rather than ask whether that meant its own
power was truly unlimited, it instead resolved

00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:15.790
to the only option it had left.

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:21.840
With a snap of its host’s fingers, the combined
creature sent the Hard to Kill Reptile away.

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:23.640
Far away.

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:29.720
Universes upon multiverses of distance were
put between the masked god and SCP-682.

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:35.320
Turning back towards the destruction it had
wrought on this world, SCP-035 knew the regenerating

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:37.370
reptile would be back.

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:41.540
But for now, it had more chaos to unfurl.

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:46.250
Now go and check out “WHAT IF SCP-096 WORE
SCP-035?”

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:50.909
for another alternative anomalous outcome
of another SCP wearing the infamous Possessive

00:20:50.909 --> 00:20:51.909
Mask!

00:20:51.909 --> 00:20:55.549
And, if you haven’t already, then why not
watch the first installment of “WHAT IF

00:20:55.549 --> 00:20:59.309
SCP-343 WORE SCP-035?”

00:20:59.309 --> 00:21:00.960
to catch up on the story so far!

